1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:06,000
This is Brand AI-Readiness Audit, a skill marketplace for AI agents.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:11,600
Give it a URL, and it explains why AI assistants don't cite that brand, and what to fix first.

3
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:18,000
Here's the architecture. Claude Code loads one entrypoint skill, audit-orchestrator.

4
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:23,500
It checks the URL is safe to audit, then crawls the site once into a shared page inventory.

5
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:29,000
Four detector skills read that inventory independently: selection, absorption, trust and engagement.

6
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:33,600
Every finding passes an advisory critic before it's composed into one report.

7
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:40,000
We treat AI visibility as a series of gates, not a single score.

8
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:46,000
A page has to clear each gate in order, and each gate has its own fix.

9
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:53,600
If a page stops at selection, more content won't help. It needs a clear entity declaration.

10
00:00:54,500 --> 00:01:00,000
Every check traces back to measured data: 602 prompts and 21,143 citations.

11
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:06,000
For example, only 76% of the pages an engine chose to cite could actually be fetched.

12
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:11,600
Each measured fact maps to a specific check in the code.

13
00:01:12,500 --> 00:01:18,000
Pages with code, numbers, definitions and comparisons shape answers more.

14
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:23,000
FAQ formatting is the one pattern that measured negative.

15
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:27,600
So the audit never tells you to add an FAQ, and a test makes sure of it.

16
00:01:28,500 --> 00:01:34,000
Thresholds sit at the bottom quartile. It's a floor, not a target.

17
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:39,600
That keeps the audit precise. It flags the pages that really fall short.

18
00:01:40,500 --> 00:01:46,000
Severity says how much a problem costs. Claim level says how sure we are.

19
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:52,000
A direct observation can be critical. An interpretation is capped at medium.

20
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:58,000
A causal promise is never reported as a finding. It's kept as a hypothesis.

21
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:03,600
That cap is checked three times: at construction, in review, and at schema validation.

22
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:10,000
Detectors are optimistic by design, so every finding has to get past a critic.

23
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:16,000
It needs a real URL and a measured value, and the value has to break the threshold.

24
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:22,000
Weak claims are dropped or downgraded, and the reason is logged in the report.

25
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:29,600
Symptoms of one cause, like a JavaScript-only page, are merged into a single fix.

26
00:02:30,500 --> 00:02:36,000
Each finding becomes an action with steps, effort, the mechanism, and a way to verify it.

27
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:42,000
Findings are sorted by severity, then pipeline order, so root causes come first.

28
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:49,600
And we'd rather add a missing fact than rewrite a page. Rewrites measurably backfired.

29
00:02:50,500 --> 00:02:59,400
Now let's run it live, with Claude Code and Claude Opus 5.5, on a site it hasn't seen.
